ary documents to give effect  to this decision  the council has received a grant payment  of 750 000 pounds from the ministry of  housing communities and local government  for a capital project to commence  immediately  51 to 57 high street market former  martin spencer site was  identified due to it being in the  council's ownership  and being in a key high street location  the recommendation in this report is for  a key decision to approve to commit  and spend 750 000 pounds of external  funding to deliver this capital  renovation project for 51-57 high street  markets the projects will include a  replacement roof and scaffolding  and soft strip out including safe  removal of asbestos and services  the project is externally funded by the  ministry of housing communities and  local government  and is required to be delivered within  the set criteria and restrictions of the  town's fund programme  this follows a recent decision to  include the 750  000 funding to the council's capital  works program  for 2021 22 and forward plan  an application for listed building  consent for the replacement of the roof  was granted on the 21st of january 2021  this was required due to the facade on  the subtle square  side of the buildings being grade two  listed  the buildings involved are included in a  joint venture with homes england  the works will be subject to formal  approving approval  being received through the joint venture  permitting the capital works in  accordance with the terms and conditions  within the agreement  the capital works will be procured in  line with the council's open invitation  to tender route  led by procurement and officers are  working hard to deliver the project in a  timely manner  this project will enable the vision for  the building to be more clearly defined  in line with any repurposing of high  street and town centre  it is proposed that the building could  form part of a portfolio of assets in a  new creative land trust  that is proposed 